# sample-full.keypro
# A full KeyPro file demonstrating the complete feature set.
# Showcases: absolute note riff notation with transposition, NNS riff annotation,
# kp-layer for split keyboard setup, kp-measure, kp-patch changes,
# kp-section markers, riff reuse by reference, and multi-hand riff annotation.
#
# Song: The House of the Rising Sun — Traditional / The Animals arrangement
# Genre: English classic rock
# Key: Am (natural minor — well-suited to demonstrating minor key transposition)
#
# Performance notes:
# - Classic arpeggiated left hand pattern throughout
# - The intro arpeggio is the signature — nail it every time
# - Patch: organ on verses, swell to strings on final chorus
# - This chart demonstrates a full keyboard split setup

{kp-version: 0.1}
{title: The House of the Rising Sun}
{artist: The Animals}
{key: Am}
{kp-scale: Minor}
{tempo: 78}
{kp-feel: Slow triplet feel — 6/8 sensibility in 4/4}
{kp-notation: absolute}
{kp-enharmonic: flats}

{kp-patch: name="Hammond Organ" program=16 channel=1}

{kp-layer: name="Right hand" range-low="C4" range-high="C7" patch="Hammond Organ"}
{kp-layer: name="Left hand" range-low="A1" range-high="B3" patch="Hammond Organ" comment="Arpeggiate — do not block chord"}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# INTRO
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

{kp-section: type="intro" label="Intro — establish arpeggio pattern"}
{kp-measure: beats=4 bars=2 label="Two bar intro vamp — set the groove"}

{kp-riff: id="intro-arpeggio" notes="A2 E3 A3 C4 E4 C4 A3 E3" label="Signature intro arpeggio" hand="left" comment="This is the heartbeat of the song — keep it steady throughout"}

{kp-riff: id="verse-melody-open" notes="A4 G4 E4 C4 D4 E4 A4" label="Opening melodic phrase" hand="right"}

[Am] [C] [D] [F]
[Am] [E7] [Am] [E7]

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# VERSE 1
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

{kp-section: type="verse" label="Verse 1"}

{kp-riff: ref="intro-arpeggio"}

There is a [Am]house in [C]New Orleans
they [D]call the Rising [F]Sun
And it's [Am]been the ruin of [C]many a poor boy
and [E7]God I know I'm [Am]one [E7]

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# VERSE 2
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

{kp-section: type="verse" label="Verse 2"}

My [Am]mother was a [C]tailor
she [D]sewed my new blue [F]jeans
My [Am]father was a [C]gambling man
down in [E7]New Or[Am]leans [E7]

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# INTERLUDE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

{kp-section: type="interlude" label="Interlude — keyboard solo"}
{kp-measure: beats=4 bars=4 label="4 bar solo — stay in Am pentatonic"}

{kp-riff: id="solo-phrase-1" notes="A4 C5 D5 E5 G5 E5 D5 C5" label="Solo phrase 1 — ascending then resolve" hand="right" comment="Play with feel — this is not a fixed melody, use as a guide"}
{kp-riff: id="solo-phrase-2" notes="E5 D5 C5 A4 G4 A4 C5 E5" label="Solo phrase 2 — descending answer" hand="right"}

{kp-riff: ref="solo-phrase-1"}
[Am] [C] [D] [F]

{kp-riff: ref="solo-phrase-2"}
[Am] [E7] [Am] [E7]

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# VERSE 3
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

{kp-section: type="verse" label="Verse 3"}

Now the [Am]only thing a [C]gambler needs
is a [D]suitcase and a [F]trunk
And the [Am]only time he's [C]satisfied
is [E7]when he's on a [Am]drunk [E7]

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# VERSE 4
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

{kp-section: type="verse" label="Verse 4"}
{kp-patch: name="Strings Pad" program=49 channel=1 comment="Swell in here — build toward the climax"}

Oh [Am]mother tell your [C]children
not to [D]do what I have [F]done
Spend your [Am]lives in sin and [C]misery
in the [E7]House of the Rising [Am]Sun [E7]

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# VERSE 5 — Final, climactic
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

{kp-section: type="verse" label="Verse 5 — Final"}
{kp-patch: name="Hammond Organ" program=16 channel=1 comment="Back to organ — full and strong for the finish"}
{kp-measure: beats=4 bars=8 feel="build" label="Final verse — build intensity throughout"}

{kp-riff: id="final-fill" notes="1 b3 4 5 b7 5 4 b3" notation="nns" label="Final verse fill — NNS, play in the feel of the key" comment="Relative notation — works in any key you've transposed to"}

Well I've got [Am]one foot on the [C]platform
the [D]other foot on the [F]train
I'm going [Am]back to New Or[C]leans
to [E7]wear that ball and [Am]chain [E7]

Well there [Am]is a house in [C]New Orleans
they [D]call the Rising [F]Sun
And it's [Am]been the ruin of [C]many a poor boy
and [E7]God I know I'm [Am]one [E7]

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# OUTRO
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

{kp-section: type="outro" label="Outro — slow decay"}
{kp-measure: beats=4 bars=4 label="Repeat arpeggio and fade — let it breathe"}

{kp-riff: ref="intro-arpeggio"}

[Am] [C] [D] [F]
[Am] [E7] [Am] [Am]
